Phase 2: WebSocket Bridge
1. Frontend opens ws://localhost:8001/ws/sessions/{id}
2. Backend creates an event emitter task that forwards Azure events to the browser
3. Frontend receives session_ready → session is live
Phase 3: Voice Interview (13 Questions)
The conversation follows a strict script defined in SYSTEM_INSTRUCTIONS inside voice_live_client.py:
Questions flow:
- Q01: Full name → Q02: Age → Q03: Country (skipped for predefined users)
- Q04: Knowledge level (beginner/intermediate/advanced)
- Q05: Dependents → Q06: High-interest debt → Q07: Debt details
- Q08: Emergency fund → Q09: Monthly income → Q09b: Monthly expenses
- TOOL CALL: recordAnswers (CALL POINT A) — returns pre-computed surplus, suggested investment, 10x/6.5x figures
- Q10: Investable amount (proposed, not asked)
- Q12: Risk scenario (emotional + financial capacity derived from one question)
- Q13: Involvement preference
- TOOL CALL: recordAnswers (CALL POINT B) — saves remaining fields
- TOOL CALL: computeAndSaveProfile — computes risk_appetite via 3x3 matrix with age adjustment, builds flags, saves profile
Phase 4: Portfolio Allocation
- Q: "What are your financial goals?" → Goals, timelines, target amounts
- TOOL CALL: computeAllocation — the deterministic engine:
1. Maps Aria's 5 risk bands to 3 anchor portfolios (Conservative/Moderate/Aggressive)
2. Builds a 7-bucket US allocation (Large Cap, Small Cap, REITs, Gold, Bond, Treasury, Cash)
3. Applies goal tilts, horizon glide path, floor, normalize
4. Rolls up to 3 classes: Equities / Debt / Commodities
5. Clamps Commodities to ~10%, applies interests/avoids
6. Computes blended expected return + feasibility check (multi-goal)
- Aria presents the exact 3 percentages + feasibility verdict
- User can negotiate (Phase 9): "I want more gold" → re-calls computeAllocation with hints
Phase 5: Save & Dashboard
- TOOL CALL: savePortfolio — writes to customerDetail.csv + creates dashboard customer record
- Backend links the portfolio to the user's email in SQLite
- User can view portfolio on the dashboard (currently disabled in Shell — only Aria mode active)
